FFFFFFFF80000000 — the sign bit replicates from the top.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SRAI replicates bit 63)")) (step (n 74) (insn "srai x20, x8, 63") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "shamt 63: 0x8000000000000001 >> 63 ARITHMETIC = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF — the sign bit replicates from the top. shamt 63: all sign, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SRAI replicates bit 63)")) (step (n 75) (insn "slli x21, x8, 0") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x8000000000000001"))) (derivation "shamt 0: 0x8000000000000001 << 0, low 64 bits kept = 0x8000000000000001 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 76) (insn "slli x21, x8, 1") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000002"))) (derivation "shamt 1: 0x8000000000000001 << 1, low 64 bits kept = 0x0000000000000002 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 77) (insn "slli x21, x8, 2") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000004"))) (derivation "shamt 2: 0x8000000000000001 << 2, low 64 bits kept = 0x0000000000000004 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 78) (insn "slli x21, x8, 4") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000010"))) (derivation "shamt 4: 0x8000000000000001 << 4, low 64 bits kept = 0x0000000000000010 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 79) (insn "slli x21, x8, 8") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000100"))) (derivation "shamt 8: 0x8000000000000001 << 8, low 64 bits kept = 0x0000000000000100 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 80) (insn "slli x21, x8, 16") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000010000"))) (derivation "shamt 16: 0x8000000000000001 << 16, low 64 bits kept = 0x0000000000010000 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 81) (insn "slli x21, x8, 32") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000100000000"))) (derivation "shamt 32: 0x8000000000000001 << 32, low 64 bits kept = 0x0000000100000000 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 82) (insn "slli x21, x8, 63") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x8000000000000000"))) (derivation "shamt 63: 0x8000000000000001 << 63, low 64 bits kept = 0x8000000000000000 — bits that pass bit 63 are discarded. shamt 63: bit 0 reaches bit 63; bit 63 leaves.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; SLLI discards off the top)")) (step (n 83) (insn "addi x10, x0, 64") (writes (write (reg "x10") (value "0x0000000000000040"))) (derivation "64 = 0b1000000: the value whose low 6 bits are 0 — the register-amount wrap corner.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 84) (insn "addi x11, x0, -1") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "The pre-write: the next step's result equals the operand itself, and the laboratory's observation vocabulary is the VISIBLE register change — x11 starts at -1 so the identity lands as a transition.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 85) (insn "srl x11, x8, x10") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0x8000000000000001"))) (derivation "D-SHAMT: only the low 6 bits of rs2 are the amount — 64 reads as 0, so x11 = X unchanged (observed as the -1 to X transition the pre-write arranged). A 7-bit reader would shift by 64; the architecture has no such read.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.2 (D-SHAMT: the low 6 bits of rs2)")) (step (n 86) (insn "addi x12, x0, -1") (writes (write (reg "x12") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF: the register whose low 6 bits are all ones — the maximum amount.") (source "RVI-RV32I §